Title: The Leopard
Order: 10
Production Code: 1x10

EXT. RUINED DESERT CASTLE - NIGHT

AMB: wind over sand, a distant caravan camp

Weeks into the desert crossing, [[Reuel Briggs]] climbs alone into a ruin to smoke and think, [[Jim Titus]] waiting below with the guns. He settles on a ledge seven hundred feet above the plain.

A low wail, not quite a cat, not quite wind. Reuel dismisses it — until he turns his head and finds a leopard crouched ten paces away, tensing to spring.

REUEL BRIGGS
(to himself, ice-calm)
No stone. No cover. Only the fall.

He braces against the ledge, weighing whether to let the animal's own weight carry them both over the edge together.

REUEL BRIGGS (CONT'D)
(shouting)
Jim! JIM!

No answer comes. The leopard gathers itself.

CHARLIE VANCE (O.S.)
(distant, then closer)
Coming, Briggs — coming!

[[Charlie Vance]], alarmed by Reuel's earlier cries carrying across the dunes, scrambles through the ruin and presses Reuel's own revolver into his hand from a window above.

SFX: three gunshots

The leopard drops. Charlie finds Jim Titus at the base of the ruin afterward, curled up, apparently sound asleep through the entire ordeal.

CHARLIE VANCE
How in God's name does a man sleep through that?

Neither of them has an answer that sits well.
